.Dd March 2026
.Dt UNJBT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm unjbt
.Nd extract and decrypt a .jbt/.rb/.orb archive
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl K Ar key | Fl -key Ar key | Fl -key-file Ar path
.Op Fl -iv Ar iv | Fl -iv-file Ar path
.Ar archive
.Ar outdir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
opens the ZIP-based archive
.Ar archive
.Pq .jbt , .rb , or .orb ,
extracts all entries into
.Ar outdir
(creating directories as needed),
then decrypts each extracted file in place using BFCodec (Blowfish-derived, CBC).
Entries that do not contain the expected 8-byte trailer or valid encrypted
blocks are skipped.
.Pp
Key and IV are required.
They can be given as hex strings
.Pq Fl K Ns / Ns Fl -key ,
.Fl -iv
(spaces ignored) or as raw binary files
.Pq Fl -key-file ,
.Fl -iv-file .
A key file must be exactly 16 bytes; an IV file must be exactly 8 bytes.
The IV as hex must be 16 hex digits (8 bytes).
.Pp
If libplist is available, binary plist files are converted to XML after
decryption.
PNG images that contain the CgBI chunk (e.g. from iOS) are optionally
repaired using
.Xr pngdefry 1
or, on macOS, with
.Nm xcrun
.Nm pngcrush
when available.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl K , Fl -key Ar key
Use
.Ar key
as the cipher key (hex string; spaces ignored).
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -key-file .
.It Fl -key-file Ar path
Read the key from the binary file
.Ar path
(exactly 16 bytes).
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -key .
.It Fl -iv Ar iv
Use
.Ar iv
as the initialization vector (16 hex digits = 8 bytes; spaces ignored).
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -iv-file .
.It Fl -iv-file Ar path
Read the IV from the binary file
.Ar path
(exactly 8 bytes).
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl -iv .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bfcodec 1 ,
.Xr jbt 1 ,
.Xr pngdefry 1
